        ":question/id": "898d4ab7-b593-5ece-8f08-6c24b9d07e0b",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "If $\\csc x = \\frac{7}{5}$, then what is $\\csc (x + 18\u03c0)$?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The period of $y=\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x$ is $2\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x=\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(x+2n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=9$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x=\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(x+2\\cdot 9\\cdot \\pi )=\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(x+18\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061x=\\frac{7}{5},$ then $\\operatorname{csc}\u2061(x+18\\pi )=\\frac{7}{5}.$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
